WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:04.920
The OWASP Top 10 provides a practical recap of common application risks:

00:00:05.140 --> 00:00:09.860
broken access control, cryptographic failures, injection, insecure design,

00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:15.520
misconfiguration, vulnerable components, authentication failures, integrity failures,

00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:18.620
logging failures, and SSRF.

00:00:18.840 --> 00:00:23.560
PCI DSS responsibilities span secure development, secure configuration,

00:00:23.780 --> 00:00:29.300
vulnerability management, access control, authentication, cardholder data protection,

00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:32.560
logging, monitoring, and risk management.

00:00:32.780 --> 00:00:35.740
Application teams contribute to many of those outcomes.

00:00:35.960 --> 00:00:40.360
Application security and payment protection are connected because payment systems depend

00:00:40.580 --> 00:00:41.620
on code,

00:00:41.840 --> 00:00:47.840
APIs, deployment pipelines, cloud services, identity systems, and operational processes.

00:00:48.060 --> 00:00:52.860
A secure payment application requires shared responsibility across technical and

00:00:53.080 --> 00:00:56.920
compliance teams. Completion of this course is awareness training.

00:00:57.140 --> 00:01:01.540
It does not constitute PCI DSS certification, assessment completion,

00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:04.400
or proof of full organizational compliance.

00:01:04.620 --> 00:01:09.740
Useful follow-on materials include OWASP references, PCI DSS v4.

00:01:09.960 --> 00:01:14.840
0 references, secure coding checklists, a payment application glossary,

00:01:15.060 --> 00:01:19.780
an OWASP-to-PCI mapping matrix, and a secure payment application checklist.

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:22.640
Use this course as a planning and awareness aid.

00:01:22.860 --> 00:01:28.620
Validate PCI DSS applicability with qualified assessment and internal compliance teams.

00:01:28.840 --> 00:01:34.200
Maintain evidence for secure development, testing, monitoring, and remediation activities.

00:01:34.420 --> 00:01:38.260
Selected PCI DSS mappings for this topic include Req.

00:01:38.480 --> 00:01:42.480
6.2 - Secure software development processes; Req.

00:01:42.700 --> 00:01:50.460
11.3 - Application vulnerability testing; Req. 12.5 - PCI DSS scope and responsibilities.
